 "equipment_type": "Air-cooled scroll chiller controller (BACnet option)",
 "applies_to": "Carrier AquaSnap 30RAP010-150 air-cooled chillers and 30RAP011-060 with Greenspeed Intelligence (R-410A, ComfortLink controls) fitted with the BACnet communication option.",
 "summary": "On the 30RAP, BACnet MS/TP comes from a UPC Open controller added to the ComfortLink chiller. Its list has about 160 objects: AVs, BVs and a few multistate values (MSV) for start/stop, emergency stop, control point, demand limit, setpoints, water temperatures, pressures, compressor and pump status, run hours, service counters and alarm state.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet MS/TP"
 ],
 "firmware": null,
 "default_device_instance": "Network number 16101 followed by the MAC address (MAC 20 gives 1610120)",
 "access_inferred": false,
 "notes": [
  "BACnet comes from the optional UPC Open controller, mounted in the main control box; object names end in _1.",
  "The Network Points List gives a point description, CCN name, read/write, units, default and range for each object; descriptions here are the printed point descriptions.",
  "The table lists multistate values as MSV (mapped as MV here), e.g. MV 1 Alarm State and MV 5 Control Method.",
  "AV 8 Control Mode codes: 1 Test, 2 Local Off, 3 CCN Off, 4 Clock Off, 5 Emergency Stop, 6 Local On, 7 CCN On, 8 Clock On, 9 Heat Enabled, 10 Pump Delay."
 ],
 "source": {
  "title": "AquaSnap 30RAP010-150 Air-Cooled Chillers and 30RAP011-060 with Greenspeed Intelligence - Controls, Start-Up, Operation, Service, and Troubleshooting (Appendix D, BACnet Communication Option, Network Points List)",
  "doc_number": "30RAP-8T",
  "revision_date": "3-23",
  "url": "https://www.shareddocs.com/hvac/docs/1005/Public/0E/30RAP-8T.pdf"
 },
 "integration": {
  "summary": "Address the UPC Open, set the MS/TP DIP switches, and set the chiller control method to CCN (Configuration > OPT2 > CTRL = 3). The BMS then starts and stops the unit with BV 4 (CHIL_S_S) and can write control point and demand limit; read control mode, leaving fluid temperature, capacity and alarm state.",
  "minimum_points": [
   {
    "ref": "BV 4",
    "name": "chil_s_s_1",
    "why": "Network start/stop"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BV 6",
    "name": "emstop_1",
    "why": "Emergency stop command"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 5",
    "name": "ctrl_pnt_1",
    "why": "Control point (leaving fluid setpoint)"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 2",
    "name": "dem_lim_1",
    "why": "Demand limit, 0-100 %"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 8",
    "name": "stat_1",
    "why": "Control mode code"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 31",
    "name": "cool_lwt_1",
    "why": "Cooler leaving fluid temperature"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 30",
    "name": "cool_ewt_1",
    "why": "Cooler entering fluid temperature"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AV 3",
    "name": "cap_t_1",
    "why": "Percent total capacity"
   },
   {
    "ref": "MV 1",
    "name": "alm_msv_1",
    "why": "Alarm state: 1 Normal, 2 Alert, 3 Alarm"
   }
  ],
  "enable": "Set the control method to CCN (Configuration > OPT2 > CTRL = 3). An external CCN device then forces CHIL_S_S (BV 4) between start and stop.",
  "heartbeat": null,
  "remote_sensors": null,
  "gotchas": [
   "Several points (pumps, head pressure, Greenspeed fan drive) depend on unit options."
  ],
  "setup": [
   "The BACnet option adds a UPC Open controller; it speaks BACnet MS/TP at 9600, 19.2k, 38.4k or 76.8k (Carrier default 76.8k), set on BAS port DIP switches DS1-DS2.",
   "For MS/TP set DS3 to enable, DS4 to E1-485 and the protocol switches DS5-DS8 to MSTP; the EIA-485 jumpers must be set to EIA-485 and 2W.",
   "MAC address from the two rotary switches (tens and ones); the controller reads switches and DIP settings only at power-up.",
   "Device instance is auto-generated as the network number (default 16101) followed by the MAC address, e.g. MAC 20 gives 1610120; change it with i-Vu Tools or a BACview.",
   "Fit a BT485 terminator on the first and last controller of the MS/TP segment."
  ]
 },
